# /etc/openexchange/gateway/<process>.env (oe-gateway.env, oe-stream.env, oe-marketdata.env, oe-projector.env): the
# process's own settings, which it reads and checks itself (every problem listed in one pass, exit 78). Prefixes:
# GATEWAY_ (oe-gateway), STREAM_ (oe-stream), MD_ (oe-marketdata), HISTORY_PROJECTOR_ (oe-projector). The driver
# mode is not set here: the unit names it (oe-worker@ external, oe-worker-embedded@ embedded) and worker-launch
# refuses an env file that says otherwise.
#
# Embedded only: the parent of the in-process driver's directory (an existing, writable directory).
#GATEWAY_DRIVER_DIR=/dev/shm
#
# The idle mode of the process's duty thread and of its embedded driver: busy_spin, backoff or sleep (unset = backoff;
# any other value is refused, 78). The key is <prefix>IDLE: GATEWAY_IDLE, STREAM_IDLE, MD_IDLE, HISTORY_PROJECTOR_IDLE.
#GATEWAY_IDLE=backoff
#
# Memory and CPU: a taskset CPU list for the process (read by worker-launch). Empty: unpinned.
CPU_SET=
#
# Secrets (database passwords, JWT secret, API keys) are files the settings name (*_FILE), owned root:openexchange
# 0640, or values in <process>.secrets.env (root:root 0600).
